      "id": "en-advisory-heatwave",
      "passed": true,
      "failures": [],
      "answer": "[ndma_heatwave_02] ## Don'ts During Extreme Heat (Source: IMD-NDMA Guidelines, Page 3)\n- Avoid going out in direct sun, especially between 12:00 noon and 3:00 PM.\n- Avoid strenuous outdoor activities when outside during peak afternoon hours.\n- Do not leave children or pets alone inside parked locked vehicles under direct sunlight.\n- Avoid cooking during peak hours; open doors and windows to ventilate cooking area adequately.\n- Avoid alcohol, tea, coffee, and carbonated soft drinks, which dehydrate the body.\n- Avoid high-protein, salty, spicy, and oily food. Do not eat stale food.\n- Avoid using incandescent light bulbs and appliances which generate unnecessary heat. ",
      "evidence_count": 3,
      "has_card": true
    },
    {
      "id": "en-advisory-coldwave",
      "passed": true,
      "failures": [],
      "answer": "[ndma_coldwave_03] ## Vulnerable Groups and Winter Shelter (Source: IMD-NDMA Guidelines, Page 1 & 3)\n- Special protection for vulnerable populations: newborn infants, elderly individuals, chronically ill persons, and homeless citizens.\n- Maintain comfortable indoor room temperature and protect children and elderly from drafts.\n- District administrations provide night shelters (Rain Baseras) equipped with blankets and hot water for homeless persons during severe cold wave.\n- Emergency assistance and shelter helplines: call National Emergency helpline 112 or Disaster helpline 1077.\n- Domestic cattle and pets protection: keep animals inside sheds at night, provide dry bedding, protect from cold winds, and increase protein/mineral rations. ",
      "evidence_count": 3,
      "has_card": true
